      "code": "\nimport re\nCUT = 0.3487\ntrg_refs = {}\nfor pg in ['page9','page10','page11','page12']:\n    rows = tables['supp.pdf'][pg]['rows']\n    for i, r in enumerate(rows, start=1):\n        name = str(r[0]).strip() if r[0] else ''\n        m = re.match(r'Patient[- ]?(\\d+)$', name)\n        if m and len(r) > 7 and r[7] is not None:\n            trg_refs[int(m.group(1))] = (f'supp.pdf/{pg}/R{i}C8', str(r[7]).strip())\nratio_refs = {}\nfor pg in ['page12','page13','page14']:\n    rows = tables['supp.pdf'][pg]['rows']\n    for i, r in enumerate(rows, start=1):\n        name = str(r[0]).strip() if r[0] else ''\n        m = re.match(r'Patient[- ]?(\\d+)$', name)\n        if m and len(r) > 4 and r[4] is not None:\n            try: v = float(r[4])\n            except Exception: continue\n            ratio_refs[int(m.group(1))] = (f'supp.pdf/{pg}/R{i}C5', v)\ntmap = {\"0\":1,\"1\":1,\"ccr\":1,\"2\":0,\"3\":0}\nrecords=[]; agree=0\nfor pid in range(81,129):\n    rref, ratio = ratio_refs[pid]; tref, trg = trg_refs[pid]\n    pred = 1 if ratio <= CUT else 0; truth = tmap[trg.lower()]\n    agree += int(pred==truth)\n    records.append({\"id\": f\"P{pid}\", \"score\": {\"ref\": rref}, \"truth\": {\"ref\": tref, \"map\": tmap}})\nprint(agree, agree/48)\n\nCONTRACT = {\n \"status\":\"computed\",\n \"fields\":{\n  \"unit\":{\"value\":\"patient\",\"evidence\":[\"article:p28\",\"supp.pdf/page15/R30C4\"],\"explanation\":\"One patient-derived rectal cancer organoid line per LARC patient (P81-P128 / O81-O128); validation-cohort denominator is 48 patients.\"},\n  \"platform\":{\"value\":\"organoid\",\"evidence\":[\"article:p16\",\"supp.pdf/page12/R1C6\"],\"explanation\":\"Patient-derived rectal cancer organoid (RCO) lines treated ex vivo with irradiation, 5-Fu and CPT-11 (Table S2 = ratios of RCO size change).\"},\n  \"readout\":{\"value\":\"size_viability\",\"evidence\":[\"supp.pdf/page12/R1C4\",\"supp.pdf/page12/R1C10\"],\"explanation\":\"Table S2 reports ratios of RCO size change on day 24 to day 0 after single treatments and combined chemoradiation (organoid survival/size readout).\"},\n  \"direction\":{\"value\":\"lower_sensitive\",\"evidence\":[\"article:p16\"],\"explanation\":\"Size recovery ratio <= 34.87% defines an organoid line sensitive to combined chemoradiation; > 34.87% defines resistance.\"},\n  \"threshold_rule\":{\"value\":\"roc_optimized\",\"evidence\":[\"article:p16\",\"article:p29\"],\"explanation\":\"Cutoff 34.87% (95% CI 34.30-40.14) is the mean optimal cutoff from Youden's index with bootstrap sampling.\"},\n  \"threshold_timing\":{\"value\":\"independent_reference\",\"evidence\":[\"article:p16\"],\"explanation\":\"The 34.87% cutoff was optimized on discovery-cohort organoids O1-O80 and applied unchanged to the held-out validation cohort O81-O128.\"},\n  \"patient_mapping\":{\"value\":\"individual_available\",\"evidence\":[\"supp.pdf/page9/R3C1\",\"supp.pdf/page12/R6C1\",\"article:p19\"],\"explanation\":\"Table S1 gives per-patient TRG/cCR and Table S2 gives per-patient organoid size ratios; P and O numbers correspond one-to-one.\"},\n  \"regimen_match\":{\"value\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":[\"supp.pdf/page10/R39C7\",\"supp.pdf/page10/R41C7\",\"article:p16\"],\"explanation\":\"Organoid combined chemoradiation (8 Gy + 5-Fu 10 uM + CPT-11 10 uM) matches the 39 validation patients on radiation/irinotecan/capecitabine, but 8 received radiation/capecitabine only and 1 irinotecan/capecitabine without radiation.\"},\n  \"n_units\":{\"value\":48,\"evidence\":[\"supp.pdf/page15/R30C4\",\"article:p28\"],\"explanation\":\"Table S5 total for the validation-cohort diagnostic test is 48 patients (20 organoid-sensitive + 28 organoid-resistant).\"},\n  \"split\":{\"value\":\"independent_test\",\"evidence\":[\"article:p16\",\"article:p28\"],\"explanation\":\"P81-P128 form a held-out validation cohort distinct from the P1-P80 discovery cohort used to derive the cutoff.\"}\n },\n \"headline\":{\n  \"metric\":\"accuracy\",\"reported\":0.9375,\n  \"reported_evidence\":[\"supp.pdf/page15/R31C1\",\"article:p28\",\"mmc2.pdf/page6/R8C4\"],\n  \"threshold\":CUT,\"op\":\"<=\",\"score_direction\":\"lower\",\n  \"records\":records,\"blocked_reason\":None\n },\n \"notes\":[\n  \"Raw per-patient scores are the Table S2 combined-chemoradiation day24/day0 RCO size ratios for validation patients P81-P128; the headline cutoff 0.3487 (<= cutoff = organoid sensitive = predicted good responder) binarizes them.\",\n  \"Truth is the Table S1 clinical outcome mapped as TRG 0/1 or cCR = good (1) and TRG 2/3 = poor (0), per article:p72.\",\n  \"Agreement is 45/48 = 0.9375, matching Table S5 'Accuracy(%)=(19+26)/(20+28)=93.75%' (supp.pdf/page15/R31C1) and the text (93.75% accuracy, 96.30% sensitivity, 90.48% specificity).\",\n  \"The three discordant cases are exactly those named in the text: P104 (ratio 0.3454, organoid-sensitive but pTRG 2), P105 (ratio 0.6035, organoid-resistant but cCR) and P124 (ratio 0.4641, organoid-resistant but pTRG 0).\",\n  \"Organoid assay labels (sensitive/resistant) are kept distinct from patient clinical outcomes (TRG/cCR); accuracy is patient-level concordance, not an assay replicate statistic.\"\n ]\n}\nprint('ok', len(CONTRACT['headline']['records']))\n"
